Package: DrumSCircle
Version: 0.1
Date: 2026-08-15
Title: Animate across possible UMAP plots
Authors@R: person(given = "Lindsay", middle = "Virginia", family = "Clark",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "Lindsay.Clark@seattlechildrens.org")
Author: Lindsay V. Clark [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Lindsay V. Clark <Lindsay.Clark@seattlechildrens.org>
Imports: umap, ggplot2, pracma, gganimate
Description: Both an art project and a reminder not to overinterpret our UMAP
  plots. Starting from a matrix of PCA coordinates or other data, multiple
  (ten by default) UMAP projections are generated, rotated to align to each
  other, and ordered by their similarity. An animation, exportable as a GIF, is
  then generated showing the observations (i.e. rows of the input matrix; cells
  if you are analyzing single cell data) moving around from projection to
  projection. Named for the eclectic dancing that one might see at a drum
  circle.
